## Root Cause
`tests/integration/home.spec.ts:9` asserts the home page's single `<h1>` reads
exactly `Corner Shop`:

```ts
expect(await page.locator('h1').textContent()).toBe('Corner Shop');
```

The only production source for that page is the inline HTML string in
`services/web/server.js` (served for every request; Playwright boots it via
`webServer.command: 'node ../services/web/server.js'` in
`tests/playwright.config.ts`). Line 10 of that file renders `<h1>Welcome</h1>`,
so `textContent()` returns `"Welcome"` — exactly the received value in the
failure output. This is the planted production defect that the file's own header
comment describes.

The sibling assertion at line 14 (`a[href]` === `/hours`) already passes and
must keep passing, so the `<a href="/hours">Opening hours</a>` element must be
left untouched.

